From 63c69153bb91ac10e0d1fba35aed9044344aa091 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: well0nez <8986239+well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 11:18:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 82/88] h713: power off through crust - the board rails off,
 the key wakes with a reset

The vendor's fake poweroff (blob 0xeaa8, doku/187) on TF-A's request 0x19
on port 3: outside a standby the phase moves to POWEROFF (TF-A's
confirmation), PB5 and PL3 go low as U-Boot's power gate leaves them, the
whole CSS goes down after 50 ms (css_power_off(): Linux parks CPU1..3 in a
loop at a power off) and the system state machine shuts down instead of
suspending. After the DRAM's self-refresh the board's rail enable goes low
(H713_POWER_OFF_RAILS_PIN, PL6: vdd-cpu, vdd-sys, vcc-pll and vcc-dram in
both stock trees). A wake raises it, waits 10 ms, turns RTC GP5 "GATE" into
"RUN1" and resets through the R_WDOG: a warm start the gate boots through.
BUILD2 bit 24 says it can. h713_hy310_sr_defconfig takes it; the test build
h713_hy310_sr_off_test_defconfig also wakes by itself after 60 s.
Built, not yet measured on a device.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
